# Lead vs worker — no drift

## Roles
- **Daniel:** owner, Approves, holds keys/media, pastes Claude tickets.
- **Cursor lead:** quarterback. Writes tickets, updates `docs/COMMAND-OS.md`, unblocks auth/ops, assigns Claude/governance/growth. Does **not** take the next Block A page family when a worker agent is assigned.
- **Cursor worker (one):** owns Block A staging page rebuilds per `diagnostics/WORKER-HANDOFF-*.md`.
- **Claude:** text/docs only. Never HTML/CSS/WP apply.

## Secrets and new-agent investment (hard)
If Daniel spent time adding or refreshing `TC_WP_USER` / `TC_WP_APP_PASSWORD` and/or launching a **new Cursor agent for staging work**, that agent owns the next Block A family.

Lead may:
1. Prove REST auth once
2. Point the worker at the handoff
3. Clear a true blocker (auth note, missing ticket)

Lead may **not**:
- Rebuild Office / Books / Lighting / Tech children “because REST works here”
- Invent a parallel page plan in chat
- Leave the worker with nothing while lead ships the same family

## Same-family ban
Never two agents on the same hub family, same Additional CSS, or same page IDs at once.

## After any ship
Update `docs/COMMAND-OS.md` § Current assignment. Commit the board with the work.
